# Example crontab for a Linux VM (e.g. Oracle Cloud Always Free, a friend's VPS, WSL).
# Runs the batch every 60 minutes; each invocation is a clean process (no sleep-loop),
# resumes from state.json, and posts the run-summary to Telegram via scripts/notify.js.
#
# Install: copy this line into `crontab -e` and adjust the path.
#   */60 * * * * cd /opt/1xauto && /usr/bin/node /opt/1xauto/scripts/scheduled-run.mjs >> /var/log/1xauto-cron.log 2>&1
#
# Also install a systemd timer if you prefer that over cron (see roadmap P7).
